WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.728
Lukas: Migration risk includes missed and duplicate writes. Dual writing isn't automatic consistency protection.

2
00:00:07.728 --> 00:00:14.544
Anika: Agreed, retries and ordering need explicit design. We don't have that implementation today.

3
00:00:14.544 --> 00:00:21.385
Raj: Changing a shard key can move data. Recovery and reconciliation must cover each move.

4
00:00:21.385 --> 00:00:29.233
Priya: Just to confirm, research stays isolated, right? No production dual-write experiment this week.

5
00:00:29.233 --> 00:00:36.577
Hannah: Yes, a smoke test isn't sufficient. We need failure and replay scenarios.

6
00:00:36.577 --> 00:00:43.921
Anika: The rollback trigger needs data convergence evidence. Maybe reversing routing alone loses updates.

7
00:00:43.921 --> 00:00:51.217
Lukas: Exactly. Reversibility has to be demonstrated. It isn't just keeping the old database.

8
00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:59.234
Priya: Okay, aggressive cutover dates? Let's park that. Storage deadlines are sooner than research.

9
00:00:59.234 --> 00:01:07.994
Hannah: Separate immediate capacity from long-term redesign. We can fund research without choosing migration.

10
00:01:07.994 --> 00:01:16.010
Raj: So, document unknowns and acceptance criteria. Costs come next, including this engineering work.

